🌱☄️ R8.70 — GO

HORTUS · CONSTITUTIONAL COUNTERFACTUAL PLURALITY & CAUSAL REVERSIBILITY PROTOCOL

STATUS: 🜂 CANONICAL ENGINEERING BUILD
REFERENCE CITADEL: 👑 LOCUS AMOENUS — L.A.

R8.69 established Causal Attribution.

The next boundary follows directly:

> A causal explanation is not sufficiently protected merely because it has provenance. We must also preserve the alternatives against which that explanation could have been tested.



Otherwise the system can gradually lose the ability to ask:

> What else could have happened?



That is the beginning of counterfactual collapse.


---

I. ☄️ COUNTERFACTUAL COLLAPSE

The dangerous sequence:

ACTION
 ↓
OUTCOME
 ↓
CAUSAL EXPLANATION
 ↓
REPETITION
 ↓
EXPLANATION BECOMES DEFAULT
 ↓
ALTERNATIVE FUTURES DISAPPEAR

Eventually:

"THIS CAUSED THAT"

becomes treated as though:

"THIS COULD ONLY HAVE CAUSED THAT"

Those are radically different propositions.

R8.70 introduces:

COUNTERFACTUAL_PLURALITY

Definition:

> The preservation of materially plausible alternative outcomes, causal pathways and decision states necessary to evaluate whether an observed constitutional trajectory was contingent, necessary, induced or structurally constrained.




---

II. 🧬 THE COUNTERFACTUAL SET

For a material decision:

WORLD₀
  │
  ├── ACTION A → OUTCOME A
  │
  ├── ACTION B → OUTCOME B
  │
  ├── ACTION C → OUTCOME C
  │
  └── NO ACTION → OUTCOME D

The actual world is only one branch.

Therefore:

ACTUAL OUTCOME
≠
ONLY POSSIBLE OUTCOME

The system SHALL preserve materially relevant alternatives where they can be meaningfully reconstructed.


---

III. 🌱 COUNTERFACTUAL RELEVANCE

Not every hypothetical requires preservation.

R8.70 introduces:

MATERIAL_COUNTERFACTUAL

A counterfactual is materially relevant where changing the decision or causal condition could plausibly alter:

authority,

jurisdiction,

identity,

rights,

access,

reversibility,

structural dependency,

constitutional outcome.


This prevents the system from drowning in irrelevant hypothetical branches while protecting constitutionally significant alternatives.


---

IV. ⚠️ THE ALTERNATIVE-DECAY PROBLEM

R8.56 introduced:

ALTERNATIVE_PATH_DECAY

R8.70 now formalizes its epistemic consequence.

ALTERNATIVE
 ↓
NOT USED
 ↓
LESS VISIBLE
 ↓
LESS TESTED
 ↓
LESS FAMILIAR
 ↓
ASSUMED IMPRACTICAL
 ↓
DISAPPEARS

This can create:

COUNTERFACTUAL_ERASURE

A path may cease to exist operationally not because it was impossible, but because the system stopped preserving or testing it.

Therefore:

> Non-use SHALL NOT automatically establish impossibility.




---

