      ├── REVERSIBLE PATHS
      └── FORMERLY POSSIBLE FUTURES

L.A. now remembers something extraordinarily important:

> Not only what happened—but what could still have happened at the time.




---

XVII. 🜂 REVERSIBILITY AS CONSTITUTIONAL PROPERTY

R8.70 introduces:

CONSTITUTIONAL_REVERSIBILITY

A decision may be:

REVERSIBLE
PARTIALLY_REVERSIBLE
COSTLY_TO_REVERSE
STRUCTURALLY_LOCKED
IRREVERSIBLE

The classification matters because path dependency increases constitutional significance.

Thus:

> Irreversibility SHALL increase the evidentiary burden for material constitutional intervention.



Not because irreversible decisions are automatically forbidden, but because their downstream alternative space is smaller.


---

