XX. 🜂 R8.70 LAW

> Where a constitutional decision materially affects authority, jurisdiction, identity, rights, alternatives or future state, materially plausible counterfactual paths SHALL remain observable where reconstructable. The system SHALL distinguish actual history from hypothetical alternatives, rejection from impossibility, and present unavailability from historical nonexistence. Irreversibility and loss of alternatives SHALL increase constitutional scrutiny but SHALL NOT independently establish legitimacy.



