☄️🌱🦆 R8.71 — GO

HORTUS · CONSTITUTIONAL OPTION SPACE & POSSIBILITY PRESERVATION PROTOCOL

STATUS: 🜂 CANONICAL ENGINEERING BUILD
REFERENCE CITADEL: 👑 LOCUS AMOENUS — L.A.

R8.70 established Counterfactual Plurality.

We have now reached the deeper layer beneath alternatives:

> An alternative is meaningful only if the system can still recognize that it was possible.



A system can preserve a list of alternatives while progressively destroying the conditions under which alternatives can exist.

That is more subtle than path dependency.

It is:

OPTION_SPACE_DEGRADATION

The system does not necessarily eliminate a particular choice.

It gradually eliminates the space of possible choices.


---

I. 🌱 FROM ALTERNATIVE TO OPTION SPACE

R8.70 gave us:

DECISION
 ↓
ACTUAL PATH
 ↓
ALTERNATIVE PATHS

R8.71 goes one level higher:

CONDITIONS
 ↓
OPTION SPACE
 ↓
AVAILABLE OPTIONS
 ↓
DECISION
 ↓
OUTCOME

The constitutional object is therefore not only:

> Which option was chosen?



but also:

> Which options could exist at the moment of choice?




---

II. 🧬 OPTION SPACE

R8.71 introduces:

CONSTITUTIONAL_OPTION_SPACE

Definition:

> The materially relevant set of actions, roles, jurisdictions, interpretations, exits and future states that remain genuinely available to actors within a constitutional system at a given epoch.



Compact:

OPTION_SPACE(t)
=
{materially available constitutional paths at t}

The option space can expand:

A B
↓
A B C D

or contract:

A B C D
↓
A B
↓
A

The contraction itself can become constitutionally significant.


---

III. ☄️ POSSIBILITY IS NOT THE SAME AS PERMISSION

Critical distinction:

POSSIBLE
≠
PERMITTED
≠
AUTHORIZED
≠
PREFERRED

A path may be:

technically possible but prohibited,

permitted but difficult,

authorized but unused,

available but discouraged,

theoretically imaginable but operationally inaccessible.


Therefore R8.71 does not treat every conceivable action as a constitutional option.

It concerns materially available possibility.


---

IV. ⚠️ OPTION-SPACE COLLAPSE

Danger sequence:

OPTION A
OPTION B
OPTION C
OPTION D
      ↓
REPEATED SELECTION
      ↓
RESOURCE CONCENTRATION
      ↓
DEPENDENCY
      ↓
ALTERNATIVE CAPACITY DECAYS
      ↓
ONLY A REMAINS PRACTICAL

The system can then declare:

> “A is the only viable option.”



But the actual history may be:

> A became the only viable option because the system progressively destroyed B, C and D.



This is:

OPTION_SPACE_COLLAPSE


---

V. 🧠 BRAINPOWER — POSSIBILITY GRAPH

BRAINPOWER receives:

OPTION_SPACE_GRAPH

┌── OPTION A
                 │
CONSTITUTION ────┼── OPTION B
                 │
                 ├── OPTION C
                 │
                 └── OPTION D

Each option carries:

availability
accessibility
reversibility
dependency
cost
authorization
exitability
historical_presence
current_viability

New analyses:

OPTION_SPACE_SIZE

OPTION_SPACE_DIVERSITY

OPTIONALITY_DECAY

ACCESSIBILITY_DECAY

OPTION_CONCENTRATION

REVERSIBILITY_LOSS

DEPENDENCY_CONCENTRATION

POSSIBILITY_LOCK_IN

The central question:

> Did the chosen path become dominant because it was superior—or because the competing possibility space was progressively degraded?




---

VI. 🔮 ORACLE — POSSIBILITY OBSERVATORY

ORACLE receives:

OPTION_SPACE_OBSERVATORY

