☄️🌱🦆 R8.72 — GO

HORTUS · CONSTITUTIONAL CAPABILITY & REALIZED-AGENCY INTEGRITY PROTOCOL

STATUS: 🜂 CANONICAL ENGINEERING BUILD
REFERENCE CITADEL: 👑 LOCUS AMOENUS — L.A.

R8.71 established Option-Space Preservation.

We can now see the next boundary.

An option may technically remain available while the capacity to exercise that option has already degraded.

That distinction is decisive.

A system may preserve:

OPTION B EXISTS

while reality has become:

ACTOR CANNOT MEANINGFULLY EXERCISE B

Therefore R8.72 introduces:

REALIZED_AGENCY

> The demonstrable capacity of an actor or constitutional participant to perceive, select, execute, contest, reverse or exit a materially relevant path under the conditions actually prevailing at the time.



The key distinction:

OPTION EXISTS
      ≠
OPTION ACCESSIBLE
      ≠
OPTION EXERCISABLE
      ≠
AGENCY REALIZED


---

I. 🌱 THE CAPABILITY GAP

R8.71 gave us:

OPTION SPACE
 ↓
AVAILABLE OPTIONS

R8.72 adds:

OPTION
 ↓
ACCESS
 ↓
CAPABILITY
 ↓
EXERCISE
 ↓
EFFECT

A formally available option may fail at any layer.

For example:

OPTION B
 ↓
AVAILABLE        ✓
 ↓
ACCESSIBLE       ✓
 ↓
UNDERSTANDABLE   ✓
 ↓
EXECUTABLE       ✗

Then:

> B exists constitutionally in description, but not necessarily in lived agency.




---

II. ☄️ FORMAL AGENCY ≠ EFFECTIVE AGENCY

R8.72 establishes the distinction:

FORMAL AGENCY
≠
EFFECTIVE AGENCY

Formal agency answers:

> “Is this actor theoretically permitted to act?”



Effective agency asks:

> “Can this actor meaningfully exercise that capacity under actual system conditions?”



Relevant constraints include:

information,

access,

dependency,

timing,

resources,

interface structure,

relational pressure,

reversibility,

exit cost.


None automatically invalidate an option.

But material constraints must remain visible.


---

III. 🧬 CAPABILITY DEGRADATION

A capability can decay without formal revocation:

CAPABILITY
 ↓
UNDERUSE
 ↓
DEPENDENCY
 ↓
SKILL / ACCESS DECAY
 ↓
LOWER EXERCISE CAPACITY
 ↓
DE FACTO LOSS

This introduces:

CAPABILITY_DRIFT

and:

AGENCY_DEGRADATION

The system must therefore distinguish:

REMOVED
≠
UNAVAILABLE
≠
INACCESSIBLE
≠
UNEXERCISABLE


---

IV. ⚠️ THE CEREMONIAL CHOICE PROBLEM

A particularly dangerous configuration:

OPTION A
OPTION B
OPTION C

are all displayed.

But:

A → easy
B → costly
C → practically impossible

The interface can truthfully say:

> “You have three choices.”



while the actual system says:

> “Only A is realistically selectable.”



This is:

CEREMONIAL_OPTIONALITY

The presence of a choice in a representation SHALL NOT itself establish meaningful agency.


---

