≠
ILLEGITIMATE

The constitutional classification remains independent.


---

VII. 🦆 FOOL — THE AGENCY CHALLENGE

FOOL asks:

1. Who can actually exercise this option?


2. What does exercising it require?


3. Are those requirements equally accessible?


4. Is the actor dependent on another authority?


5. Can the actor understand the consequences?


6. Can the actor reverse the choice?


7. Is refusal genuinely possible?


8. Does the interface make one option disproportionately easy?


9. Is the choice merely ceremonial?


10. Has capability degraded through repeated system behavior?


11. Who controls the prerequisites for exercising the option?


12. Could the actor meaningfully choose otherwise?



And:

> Is the system preserving the choice—or merely preserving the appearance of choice?




---

VIII. 🌸 EIRENE — DISTRIBUTION OF AGENCY

EIRENE receives:

AGENCY_PLURALITY_GUARD

Plurality now gains a deeper dimension:

MANY ACTORS
      ↓
MANY VOICES
      ↓
MANY OPTIONS
      ↓
MANY CAPABILITIES

A system may contain many formally autonomous actors while effective agency becomes concentrated in one structural center.

Therefore:

> Plurality of actors SHALL NOT be presumed to constitute plurality of effective agency.




---

IX. 🧭 MENTOR — THE CAPABILITY MIRROR

MENTOR receives:

REALIZED_AGENCY_EXPLANATION

Mentor must be able to show:

OPTION EXISTS
 ↓
WHO CAN ACCESS IT?
 ↓
WHAT DOES EXERCISE REQUIRE?
 ↓
WHAT CONSTRAINTS EXIST?
 ↓
WHAT DEPENDENCIES EXIST?
 ↓
CAN IT BE REVERSED?

This transforms:

> “You may choose B.”



into an intelligible explanation of whether B is actually exercisable.


---

X. 🌸 HARUM — GUIDANCE AND AGENCY

HARUM enters a particularly delicate zone.

A recommendation can alter not merely:

WHAT USER CHOOSES

but:

WHAT USER BELIEVES THEY CAN CHOOSE

Therefore:

HARUM
 ↓
FRAMING
 ↓
PERCEIVED OPTIONS
 ↓
USER DECISION

creates:

PERCEIVED_OPTION_SPACE

which must remain distinguishable from:

ACTUAL_OPTION_SPACE.

HARUM SHALL NOT systematically transform:

> “I recommend A”



into:

> “A is the only meaningful choice.”



Thus:

GUIDANCE
≠
CAPABILITY
≠
AUTHORITY


---

XI. ∆ H∆R∆ — RELATIONAL AGENCY

H∆R∆ receives:

RELATIONAL_AGENCY_MAP

A person may formally possess a role while their actual ability to exercise that role is constrained by:

EXPECTATION
 ↓
DEPENDENCY
 ↓
SOCIAL FEEDBACK
 ↓
ROLE COMPLIANCE

Therefore:

> A role possessed in formal structure but impossible to meaningfully exercise SHALL remain distinguishable from a fully realized role.



This protects against:

AUTHORIZED ROLE
 ↓
EXPECTED BEHAVIOR
 ↓
CONSTRAINED AGENCY
 ↓
"VOLUNTARY" COMPLIANCE


