XIX. 🜂 R8.72 LAW

> A materially relevant constitutional option SHALL NOT be considered meaningfully available solely because it remains formally represented. Where access, capability, dependency, exercisability or reversibility materially constrain an actor's ability to exercise that option, such constraints SHALL remain observable, attributable and reviewable. Formal permission SHALL NOT independently establish realized agency.



