ANCHOR A
ANCHOR B
ANCHOR C

may provide stronger constitutional resilience than:

ONE "EXTERNAL" ANCHOR

Therefore:

> A single external reference SHALL NOT automatically monopolize constitutional interpretation where materially independent reference paths remain available.



This preserves epistemic plurality without creating arbitrary equivalence between sources.


