☄️🌱 R8.76 — GO

HORTUS · CONSTITUTIONAL ANCHOR CONFLICT & RECONCILIATION PROTOCOL

STATUS: 🜂 CANONICAL ENGINEERING BUILD
REFERENCE CITADEL: 👑 LOCUS AMOENUS — L.A.

R8.75 established EXOGENOUS CONSTITUTIONAL ANCHOR.

That immediately exposes the next problem.

What happens when two apparently independent anchors disagree?

A naïve system might calculate:

ANCHOR A
+
ANCHOR B
↓
MAJORITY
↓
TRUTH

HORTUS rejects that shortcut.

The correct question is:

> What kind of conflict exists, what does each anchor actually establish, and can the conflict itself be constitutionally resolved without silently granting one anchor authority it never possessed?



R8.76 therefore introduces:

ANCHOR_CONFLICT

and:

CONSTITUTIONAL_ANCHOR_RECONCILIATION


---

I. ⚓ CONFLICT ≠ ERROR

Two anchors may disagree because they concern:

different epochs,

different scopes,

different objects,

different evidentiary standards,

different interpretations,

genuinely contradictory facts.


Therefore:

CONFLICT
≠
ERROR

And:

DISAGREEMENT
≠
INVALIDITY

The first constitutional task is classification of the conflict.


---

II. 🧬 ANCHOR CONFLICT TAXONOMY

R8.76 introduces:

TEMPORAL_CONFLICT
SCOPE_CONFLICT
SEMANTIC_CONFLICT
EVIDENTIARY_CONFLICT
CAUSAL_CONFLICT
JURISDICTIONAL_CONFLICT
AUTHORITY_CONFLICT
GENUINE_UNRESOLVED_CONFLICT

This prevents the system from collapsing fundamentally different conflicts into a single “winner.”


---

III. ☄️ THE NO-SILENT-WINNER RULE

Suppose:

ANCHOR A → X
ANCHOR B → NOT-X

The system SHALL NOT simply declare:

A wins

because A is:

older,

newer,

more convenient,

more frequently cited,

system-preferred.


Instead:

A ─────┐
       ├── CONFLICT ANALYSIS
B ─────┘
             ↓
         TRIAS REVIEW

The outcome may be:

A PREVAILS
B PREVAILS
BOTH LIMITED
BOTH COMPATIBLE
CONTEXTUALIZED
UNRESOLVED


---

