 ↓
EXPECTATION
 ↓
PRECEDENT
 ↓
DE FACTO AUTHORITY

The original decision may have been legitimate as a bounded response to uncertainty.

Its repeated use does not automatically make it legitimate as a permanent constitutional rule.

R8.78 therefore introduces:

PROVISIONAL_CONSTITUTIONAL_AUTHORITY

with the decisive boundary:

PROVISIONAL ≠ PRECEDENTIAL


---

I. ⏳ TEMPORARY ACTION MUST HAVE A TEMPORAL IDENTITY

A provisional measure requires more than a label.

It requires:

START
 ↓
PURPOSE
 ↓
SCOPE
 ↓
CONDITIONS
 ↓
EXPIRY
 ↓
REVIEW

Therefore:

> Every materially provisional constitutional measure SHALL possess an explicit temporal and jurisdictional boundary.



No indefinite temporary state.


