VII. 🦆 FOOL — THE TEMPORAL CHALLENGE

FOOL asks:

1. When was this authority created?


2. Why was it created?


3. What uncertainty justified it?


4. What was its original scope?


5. What was its expiry condition?


6. Has that condition disappeared?


7. How many times has it been reused?


8. Has anyone explicitly adopted it as precedent?


9. Has dependency formed around it?


10. Would reversal now be politically, technically or socially difficult?


11. Has temporary necessity become permanent convenience?


12. Who benefits from keeping the exception alive?



And:

> Did the exception survive because it remained necessary—or because everyone became accustomed to it?




