☄️🌱🦆 R8.79 — GO

HORTUS · CONSTITUTIONAL REVERSAL, DE-ENTRENCHMENT & AUTHORITY DECAY PROTOCOL

STATUS: 🜂 CANONICAL ENGINEERING BUILD
REFERENCE CITADEL: 👑 LOCUS AMOENUS — L.A.

R8.78 established that provisional authority cannot become permanent merely through persistence.

But that leaves one deeper problem:

> What if persistence has already created dependency?



Because after sufficient time, simply declaring:

EXPIRE

may no longer be enough.

The system may have reorganized itself around the provisional measure.

Thus:

PROVISIONAL
 ↓
REPETITION
 ↓
DEPENDENCY
 ↓
LOCK-IN
 ↓
REVERSAL COST

R8.79 therefore introduces:

CONSTITUTIONAL_DETRENCHMENT

and:

AUTHORITY_DECAY

The fundamental principle:

> Authority that loses its constitutional basis must be capable of decaying and being safely reversed, even when the system has adapted around it.




---

I. 🧬 AUTHORITY HAS A LIFE-CYCLE

R8.79 models constitutional authority as:

CREATION
 ↓
VALIDATION
 ↓
OPERATION
 ↓
REVIEW
 ↓
RENEWAL / REVISION
 ↓
DECAY
 ↓
EXPIRY / REVERSAL

Authority is therefore not assumed to be immortal.

EXISTENCE
≠
PERPETUITY


---

II. ☄️ AUTHORITY DECAY

A constitutional authority may lose validity through:

expiry,

changed circumstances,

failed assumptions,

superseding constitutional rules,

loss of jurisdiction,

withdrawal of authorization,

evidence invalidation,

structural transformation.


R8.79 introduces:

AUTHORITY_DECAY_STATE

VALID
 ↓
AGING
 ↓
CONTESTED
 ↓
DEGRADED
 ↓
EXPIRING
 ↓
EXPIRED

Not every authority must pass through every state.

But every authority must remain capable of status change.


---

III. ⚠️ ENTRENCHMENT ≠ LEGITIMACY

The dangerous equation is:

DEPENDENCY
+
REVERSAL COST
↓
"THEREFORE IT MUST REMAIN"

HORTUS rejects this.

Instead:

DEPENDENCY
 ↓
RISK SIGNAL
 ↓
DE-TRENCHMENT ANALYSIS

Therefore:

> The difficulty of removing authority SHALL NOT itself constitute evidence that the authority remains legitimate.




---

IV. 🧠 BRAINPOWER — ENTRENCHMENT GRAPH

BRAINPOWER receives:

