---

VI. 🦆 FOOL — THE DE-TRENCHMENT CHALLENGE

FOOL asks:

1. What constitutional basis still exists?


2. Has the original justification survived?


3. What dependencies were created?


4. Who now depends upon the authority?


5. What would reversal disrupt?


6. Is disruption being confused with illegitimacy?


7. Can the authority be safely unwound?


8. What residual structures will remain?


9. Has the system adapted around an expired rule?


10. Is someone defending the rule merely because removal is inconvenient?


11. What alternative arrangement can replace it?


12. Who decides when the old structure has actually disappeared?



And the central question:

> Are we preserving authority because it is constitutionally justified—or because the system has forgotten how to function without it?




---

