R8.81 therefore formalizes:

CONSTITUTIONAL_SUCCESSION

and:

AUTHORITY_HANDOVER

The central distinction:

SUCCESSION
≠
INHERITANCE

HANDOVER
≠
AUTHORITY_CREATION

CONTINUITY
≠
TRANSFER OF ALL POWERS

A successor may inherit responsibilities, evidence, obligations and state, without automatically inheriting every authority possessed by its predecessor.


---

I. 🧬 SUCCESSION OBJECT

R8.81 introduces:

SUCCESSION_OBJECT

with four separate dimensions:

STATE
EVIDENCE
OBLIGATION
AUTHORITY

Each must be classified independently.

Thus:

OLD STATE
 ├── identity → MAY SURVIVE
 ├── history → SURVIVES
 ├── evidence → SURVIVES
 ├── obligations → REVIEW / TRANSFER
 └── authority → EXPLICITLY CLASSIFY

This blocks the dangerous shortcut:

> “Everything belonging to the old authority automatically belongs to the successor.”




