XX. 🜂 R8.83 LAW

> Where constitutional authority ends and no independently validated successor exists, the resulting absence SHALL remain a recognized constitutional vacuum. No actor SHALL acquire authority merely by occupying that vacuum. Necessary containment actions MAY occur only within explicit, bounded, temporary, provenance-traceable and independently reviewable limits. Persistence of emergency action, operational necessity or repeated practice SHALL NOT itself convert containment into constitutional authority.



