The governing principle:

> A mechanism created to preserve constitutional space SHALL NOT become the owner of that space merely because it successfully preserved it.




---

I. 🌱 VACUUM EXIT ≠ AUTHORITY CREATION

A vacuum has three possible constitutional trajectories:

VACUUM
  │
  ├── RESTORATION
  │
  ├── VALID SUCCESSION
  │
  └── RECONSTITUTION

These are different processes.

RESTORATION

The original authority returns under its still-valid constitutional basis.

SUCCESSION

A previously validated successor assumes bounded authority.

RECONSTITUTION

A new authority structure is constitutionally established because the old structure can no longer legitimately return.

None may occur merely because an interim actor has become useful.


---

II. ⚠️ THE CUSTODIAN TRAP

R8.84 identifies:

CUSTODIAN_AUTHORITY_DRIFT

Pattern:

NO AUTHORITY
 ↓
CUSTODIAN APPOINTED
 ↓
CUSTODIAN PRESERVES SYSTEM
 ↓
SYSTEM DEPENDS ON CUSTODIAN
 ↓
CUSTODIAN BECOMES NECESSARY
 ↓
"THEREFORE CUSTODIAN SHOULD GOVERN"

This inference is prohibited.

> Necessity of a custodian does not establish constitutional entitlement to govern.




---

III. ☄️ TEMPORARY MECHANISM BOUNDARY

Any vacuum-preserving mechanism SHALL have:

SCOPE
PURPOSE
DURATION
TRIGGER
EXIT CONDITION
REVIEW PATH
PROVENANCE

A temporary authority without an exit condition is constitutionally incomplete.

Therefore:

TEMPORARY
≠
UNLIMITED

and:

TEMPORARY + PERSISTENCE
≠
PERMANENT

without independent reconstitution.


---

