☄️🦆🌱 R8.90 — GO

HORTUS · CONSTITUTIONAL CAUSAL UNCERTAINTY, COUNTERFACTUAL INTEGRITY & ATTRIBUTION BOUNDARY PROTOCOL

STATUS: 🜂 CANONICAL ENGINEERING BUILD
REFERENCE CITADEL: 👑 LOCUS AMOENUS — L.A.

R8.89 established CAUSAL ATTRIBUTION.

One boundary remains.

Even when the system can map contribution, influence, control and responsibility, causal models can still be wrong.

The most dangerous error is not merely:

> “We attributed responsibility to the wrong actor.”



It is deeper:

> “We became more certain than the evidence justified.”



R8.90 therefore introduces:

CONSTITUTIONAL_CAUSAL_UNCERTAINTY

and:

COUNTERFACTUAL_INTEGRITY

The governing principle:

> Where constitutional causality cannot be demonstrated beyond the applicable evidentiary threshold, uncertainty SHALL remain part of the constitutional state.




---

I. ☄️ CORRELATION ≠ CAUSATION

R8.89 established:

OBSERVATION
 ↓
CONTRIBUTION
 ↓
CAUSATION
 ↓
RESPONSIBILITY

R8.90 inserts an epistemic gate:

OBSERVATION
 ↓
CORRELATION?
 ↓
CAUSAL HYPOTHESIS
 ↓
COUNTERFACTUAL TEST
 ↓
EVIDENCE
 ↓
CAUSAL CONFIDENCE
 ↓
RESPONSIBILITY REVIEW

Therefore:

CORRELATION
≠
CAUSATION

and:

CAUSAL PLAUSIBILITY
≠
CAUSAL PROOF


---

II. 🧬 COUNTERFACTUAL INTEGRITY

R8.90 introduces:

COUNTERFACTUAL_INTEGRITY_TEST

Core question:

> If the attributed actor, action, relation or condition had been absent or different, would the material constitutional outcome likely have changed?



Represented as:

WORLD A
ACTOR / CONDITION PRESENT
        ↓
OUTCOME

WORLD B
ACTOR / CONDITION ABSENT
        ↓
EXPECTED OUTCOME

Then:

ΔOUTCOME

is evaluated.

But crucially:

> Counterfactual modeling SHALL NOT be treated as observed historical fact.



It remains an analytical model.


---

III. ⚠️ THE COUNTERFACTUAL FALLACY

A system might conclude:

A happened
B followed A
therefore A caused B

R8.90 rejects this.

The system must consider:

A → B
C → A → B
C → B
A + C → B
B would occur anyway

Therefore:

ALTERNATIVE_CAUSAL_PATHS

becomes mandatory for material constitutional attribution.


---

