XX. 🜂 R8.91 LAW

> Constitutional decisions SHALL be supported by evidence sufficient for their consequence and authority. Evidentiary sufficiency SHALL remain distinct from observation, inference, authenticity and persistence. Thresholds SHALL be proportionate, independently reviewable and resistant to outcome-driven adjustment. Material uncertainty, evidentiary conflict and inferential distance SHALL remain visible. A decision SHALL NOT claim greater epistemic certainty than its evidence permits, and material new evidence SHALL preserve the possibility of reopening prior determinations.



