XIX. 🜂 R8.92 LAW

> A constitutionally validated decision SHALL remain distinguishable from the dependencies, adaptations and structural effects that subsequently arise from its implementation. Decision-induced persistence, dependency, alternative loss or reversal cost SHALL NOT independently increase constitutional authority or establish retroactive necessity. Where entrenchment materially changes constitutional consequences, the decision SHALL remain subject to revalidation, challenge and, where required, reversal.



