Because a system may have changed so substantially that simply saying “revalidate the old constitution” becomes conceptually insufficient.

The system may now contain:

transformed roles,

changed authority topology,

altered jurisdictions,

new identities,

new dependencies,

new relational structures,

and new constitutional expectations.


Therefore R8.96 introduces:

CONSTITUTIONAL_IDENTITY_CONTINUITY

and:

RECONSTITUTIONALIZATION

The central distinction:

> A changed constitutional state must remain distinguishable from both the state that preceded it and the process by which it becomes a new validated state.




