☄️🦆🌱 R8.97 — GO

HORTUS · RECONSTITUTION INTEGRITY, CONSTITUTIONAL SUCCESSION & AUTHORITY NON-INHERITANCE PROTOCOL

STATUS: 🜂 CANONICAL ENGINEERING BUILD
REFERENCE CITADEL: 👑 LOCUS AMOENUS — L.A.

R8.96 established the constitutional identity test:

> Is the transformed system still the same constitutional state—or has a new constitutional identity emerged?



R8.97 now addresses the next danger.

If a new constitutional identity emerges, how does authority move—or not move—between the old and new states?

Because:

OLD IDENTITY
     ↓
RECONSTITUTION
     ↓
NEW IDENTITY

creates a temptation:

> “The new state inherits everything the old state possessed.”



R8.97 rejects that assumption.

It introduces:

CONSTITUTIONAL_SUCCESSION

and the stronger invariant:

AUTHORITY_NON_INHERITANCE


---

I. ⚖️ IDENTITY SUCCESSION ≠ AUTHORITY SUCCESSION

A new constitutional identity may inherit:

historical records,

infrastructure,

evidence,

relationships,

obligations,

institutional memory.


But authority requires independent constitutional grounding.

Therefore:

IDENTITY SUCCESSION
≠
AUTHORITY SUCCESSION

and:

HISTORICAL CONTINUITY
≠
AUTOMATIC POWER CONTINUITY


---

II. ☄️ THE AUTHORITY INHERITANCE FALLACY

The dangerous sequence:

STATE₀ HAS AUTHORITY
       ↓
STATE₁ EMERGES
       ↓
STATE₁ CLAIMS SUCCESSION
       ↓
STATE₁ INHERITS ALL AUTHORITY

R8.97 inserts a mandatory gate:

STATE₁
 ↓
AUTHORITY INVENTORY
 ↓
PROVENANCE
 ↓
CONSTITUTIONAL BASIS
 ↓
TRIAS REVIEW
 ↓
AUTHORIZED / NOT AUTHORIZED

Thus:

> No authority crosses a constitutional succession boundary merely because it existed before the boundary.




---

III. 🧬 AUTHORITY LINEAGE

Every material authority claim receives:

AUTHORITY_LINEAGE

