XX. 🜂 R9.10 LAW

> A constitutional system SHALL distinguish dependency from authority and technical reversibility from meaningful exitability. Where repeated use, adaptation or structural dependence materially reduces legitimate alternatives or makes exit practically unavailable, the resulting lock-in SHALL remain observable, provenance-traceable and subject to independent constitutional review. Dependency, usefulness, persistence or practical necessity SHALL NOT independently establish constitutional legitimacy or permanence.



